SetReplicasUnusedInit	inadmissible	the nil-init of o.Labels is not written through (grammar P6, purity §4)
SetReplicasValidated	inadmissible	if n < 0 is not a nil guard that panics, the guard on the error of a local, or a nil-init guard (grammar S8, purity §4)
SetReplicasViaAddr	inadmissible	pp := &o is not v, err := json.Marshal(P) with two new names and P a parameter other than the object (grammar S3, purity §4)
SetReplicasViaAlias	inadmissible	a declaration is neither an if nor an assignment (grammar S1, purity §4)
SetReplicasViaClosure	inadmissible	contains a function literal; its body is not checked, so sugar has none (grammar S9, purity §4)
SetReplicasZero	inadmissible	new(int32) is written to o.Spec.Replicas, and new(int32) is neither an argument passed whole nor a struct literal of arguments and constants (grammar V1, purity §4)
SetSpecNestedNil	inadmissible	o.Spec is assigned Spec{…}, whose Ref is nil by name (grammar V1, purity §4)
SetSpecWithNilRef	inadmissible	o.Spec is assigned Spec{…}, whose Ref is nil by name (grammar V1, purity §4)
SetViaDelegate	inadmissible	the call statement SetName(o, n) is neither an if nor an assignment (grammar S1, purity §4)
